<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What a cloud backup may take, on Android 11 and below. Android 12 and above
    read data_extraction_rules.xml beside this, which says the same thing in the
    newer format - both are needed because the app runs from API 23.

    What is left is the settings file, and that is the whole of it: the theme,
    the reading language, which translation provider is chosen and how long it
    may take. Small, dull, and genuinely worth carrying to a new phone.

    Everything else is excluded, for reasons that are separate but point the
    same way.

    The copies of the books, because they are the reader's own files rather than
    the app's, they are megabytes each, and a backup over the 25 MB quota is not
    a partial backup - it is no backup at all, so including them would lose the
    settings too.

    The database, because it holds the passages that have been translated, which
    are the book itself, and cover images with them. This app's whole claim is
    that what it reads stays on the device, and a nightly upload of the reader's
    book to somebody's servers is not that. Backing it up would also restore
    badly: the shelf and the reading positions are keyed by where each file was,
    and with the files excluded above they would come back pointing at documents
    the new device does not have.

    The encrypted secrets, because the key that decrypts them is in this
    device's keystore and does not travel. Restored elsewhere they are bytes
    nobody can read, so excluding them means the app asks for the API key again
    rather than discovering mid-request that it cannot use the one it has.

    The crash report, because it is written for the reader to read once and
    delete, and has no business outliving the device it was written on.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="documents/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="incoming/" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="last-crash.txt" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lukia.db" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lukia.db-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lukia.db-shm" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="lukia.db-journal" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="io.lukia.secrets.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
